#. type: Title #
#: theme/README.md:1
#, no-wrap
msgid "Quarkus Roq theme"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: theme/README.md:4
#, no-wrap
msgid "The look of quarkus.io, packaged as a [Roq](https://iamroq.dev/) theme so other sites can use it.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: theme/README.md:6
#, no-wrap
msgid "It provides:\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: theme/README.md:17
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"the `base` layout (`templates/theme-layouts/quarkus/base.html`), with `lang`, `head`, `header`, `footer`\n"
"and `scripts` sections that sites can override,\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: theme/README.md:17
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"the header with the main navigation, call to action, language switcher and colour mode toggle\n"
"(`templates/partials/quarkus/header.html`); the menus are part of the theme, so they are the same on every site\n"
"using it, and their links point at https://quarkus.io/ unless `quarkus-website-theme.links-url` is set (quarkus.io,\n"
"and the localized sites built from this repository, set it to `/` so the links stay on the site),\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: theme/README.md:17
#, no-wrap
msgid "the project footer and the minimal (Commonhaus) footer,\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: theme/README.md:17
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"the colours, colour modes (light, dark, system), grid and global styles, and the header and footer styles\n"
"(`web/app/`),\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: theme/README.md:17
#, no-wrap
msgid "the logos, `colormode.js` and `mobile-nav.js` (`public/assets/`).\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: theme/README.md:18
#, no-wrap
msgid "How quarkus.io uses it"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: theme/README.md:23
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"quarkus.io adds `theme/src/main/resources` to its resources (see the root `pom.xml`), so `./serve.sh` needs no\n"
"pre-build and theme changes hot-reload like any site file. `templates/layouts/base.html` overrides the theme\n"
"`base` layout to add the site head (meta, CSP, search, tracking), the community site banner and the guide scripts.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: theme/README.md:26
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"`theme/pom.xml` packages the same sources as a jar. Since quarkus.io never uses that jar, `example-minimal-site/` is a minimal\n"
"site built against it on every pull request (see the `theme` job in `.github/workflows/build.yml`).\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: theme/README.md:27
#, no-wrap
msgid "Using the theme in another site"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: theme/README.md:30
#, no-wrap
msgid "The jar is published in a Maven repository at https://quarkus.io/maven/ on every deploy:\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced code block (xml)
#: theme/README.md:31
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<repositories>\n"
"    <repository>\n"
"        <id>quarkus-website</id>\n"
"        <url>https://quarkus.io/maven/</url>\n"
"        <snapshots><enabled>true</enabled></snapshots>\n"
"    </repository>\n"
"</repositories>\n"
"\n"
"<dependency>\n"
"    <groupId>io.quarkus</groupId>\n"
"    <artifactId>quarkus-website-theme</artifactId>\n"
"    <version>1.0.0-SNAPSHOT</version>\n"
"</dependency>\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: theme/README.md:48
#, no-wrap
msgid "Then, in the site:\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: theme/README.md:56
#, no-wrap
msgid "use `layout: base` (or a layout based on it) for pages; the jar sets `site.theme=quarkus`,\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: theme/README.md:56
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"add the theme styles to a stylesheet in `web/` with `@use \"quarkus-theme\";` (`web/app/_quarkus-theme.scss` lists the\n"
"theme stylesheets). It is a Sass partial, which isn't bundled on its own, so each site decides where the theme\n"
"styles go relative to its own, usually first so the site styles can build on them, like quarkus.io's\n"
"`web/main.scss`,\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: theme/README.md:56
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"provide the footer content in `projectfooter.yaml`, in the site data dir: `footer_text`, `links` and\n"
"`more_links`, see quarkus.io's `_data/projectfooter.yaml`.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: theme/README.md:58
#, no-wrap
msgid "`example-minimal-site/` is a complete minimal site.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: theme/README.md:59
#, no-wrap
msgid "Developing the theme"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: theme/README.md:62
#, no-wrap
msgid "Run `./serve.sh` (or `./serve-noguides.sh`) at the repository root and edit the files in `theme/src/main/resources`.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: theme/README.md:64
#, no-wrap
msgid "To check the packaged jar like CI does:\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced code block (sh)
#: theme/README.md:65
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"./mvnw -f theme/pom.xml install\n"
"cd theme/example-minimal-site && QUARKUS_ROQ_GENERATOR_BATCH=true ../../mvnw package quarkus:run -DskipTests\n"
"./verify.sh target/roq\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: theme/README.md:72
#, no-wrap
msgid "Keep in mind that a site using the jar differs from quarkus.io:\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: theme/README.md:76
#, no-wrap
msgid "the jar needs `META-INF/beans.xml`, otherwise its templates and web assets are ignored,\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: theme/README.md:76
#, no-wrap
msgid "templates use the alternative expression syntax (`{=expr}`), which `templates/.qute` enables for the jar,\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: theme/README.md:76
#, no-wrap
msgid "sites may use Qute strict rendering: guard optional data with `??`,\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: theme/README.md:76
#, no-wrap
msgid "styles reference theme images by URL, which `application.properties` keeps out of the bundling.\n"
msgstr ""
